BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Cantor Arts] Animal\, Vegetable\, nor Mineral: Works by Miljohn R
 uperto
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260802
DTSTAMP:20260729T220005Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-52888406473919-52888573116792@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Animal\, Vegetable\, nor Mineral is the first large-scale solo
  museum exhibition of Manila-born\, Los Angeles-based artist Miljohn Ruper
 to (b. 1971). Working across photography\, video\, animation\, generative 
 artificial intelligence\, and other mediums\, Ruperto explores the ways hu
 mans have understood their place in the world. From digitally-created fant
 astical botanical specimens printed as gelatin silver photographs to immer
 sive apocalyptic landscapes experienced in VR\, Ruperto’s artworks highl
 ight\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://museum.stanford.edu/exhibitions/an
 imal-vegetable-nor-mineral-works-miljohn-ruperto\nLast synced: 2026-07-29 
 15:00 PDT
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center
URL:https://museum.stanford.edu/exhibitions/animal-vegetable-nor-mineral-w
 orks-miljohn-ruperto
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Cantor Arts] JANE! An intimate exploration of Gilded Age excess 
  and the enigmatic life and death of Jane Stanford
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260802
DTSTAMP:20260729T220005Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-52880326677126-52880513697536@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Curated by Associate Curator of European Art\, Patrick R. Crow
 ley\, JANE! celebrates the aesthetic and affective excesses of Jane Stanfo
 rd\, the Gilded Age founder and matriarch of Stanford University. Bringing
  together precious keepsakes\, souvenirs\, archaeological detritus\, and s
 pooky messages from beyond the grave\, the exhibition reveals the campy un
 derside of a familiar biography and perhaps an even more familiar murder m
 ystery.\n\nFrom her elegant French gowns to a colossal painting of her jew
 els\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://museum.stanford.edu/exhibitions/jan
 e\nLast synced: 2026-07-29 15:00 PDT
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center
URL:https://museum.stanford.edu/exhibitions/jane
END:VEVENT
